For Production, we are using nginx server in prod docker image. In dev we use default node server available in our
local machine. so if there is something that is working in dev mode but in prod mode it is not working then we can fix issues for production in -

Nginx.conf file -

- If issue is about routing then fix here (react outer needs fallback path)
  location / {
  try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
  }
- static assets return 404 - fix nginx asset path configuration (dev server serves diffrently)
- CORS /wrong api url - fix Nginx proxy rules (dev server proxies diffrently)

What to review besides Nginx -
1- vite.config.ts - path and build settings differ from dev
2- .env.production - API endpoints must be embedded at build (in dev, we use localhost)
VITE_API_URL=https://domain.com/api
then use it in code like -
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL;
3- Dockerfile - ensure correct build enviornment
